wifi: mt76: mt7925: track valid BSS TX power before reporting

mt7925 stores per-BSS TX power once mac80211 sends BSS_CHANGED_TXPOWER.
Before that event, dev->phy.txpower is still the zero-initialized value,
but mt7925_mcu_set_rate_txpower() treats it as a valid configured power
and feeds 0 into mt76_get_power_bound(). This leaves phy->txpower_cur at
0 and makes userspace report txpower 0.00 dBm after reload or while
disconnected.

Track whether the per-BSS TX power has actually been received. Until it
has, fall back first to hw->conf.power_level and then to the current
channel regulatory max power before entering the existing mt76 power
bound and rate power limit path. Once mac80211 has sent BSS TX power,
use it as-is, including a legitimate 0 dBm value.

Signed-off-by: Darafei Praliaskouski <me@komzpa.net>
Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <floss@jetm.me>

9bc2b5de9b8cccf771ed6718ce6b99ff4fdb1df8
diff --git a/mt7925/main.c b/mt7925/main.c
index 9f269e2..0d3d066 100644
--- a/mt7925/main.c
+++ b/mt7925/main.c
@@ -2127,4 +2127,5 @@ static void mt7925_link_info_changed(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_TXPOWER &&
-	    info->txpower != phy->txpower) {
+	    (!phy->txpower_set || info->txpower != phy->txpower)) {
 		phy->txpower = info->txpower;
+		phy->txpower_set = true;
 		mt7925_mcu_set_rate_txpower(phy->mt76);
diff --git a/mt7925/mcu.c b/mt7925/mcu.c
index 6f19a97..2c5b625 100644
--- a/mt7925/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7925/mcu.c
@@ -3935,4 +3935,8 @@ int mt7925_mcu_set_rate_txpower(struct mt76_phy *phy)
 
-		tx_power = mt76_get_power_bound(phy,
-						dev->phy.txpower);
+		tx_power = dev->phy.txpower_set ? dev->phy.txpower :
+						  mdev->hw->conf.power_level;
+		if (!tx_power)
+			tx_power = phy->chandef.chan->max_power;
+
+		tx_power = mt76_get_power_bound(phy, tx_power);
 		tx_power = mt76_get_rate_power_limits(phy,
diff --git a/mt792x.h b/mt792x.h
index f067cb3..0e74f0c 100644
--- a/mt792x.h
+++ b/mt792x.h
@@ -171,2 +171,3 @@ struct mt792x_phy {
 	int txpower;
+	bool txpower_set;
 
